2:["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 bg-accent-1-muted p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"caption-lg","children":"Poor Handoffs"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"There existed no system in place for developers to create new elements, instead trying to replicate what the previous developer had done with no context."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 bg-accent-2-muted p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"caption-lg","children":"Inconsistent Designs"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Without a proper system for creating elements in Wiz Parser, the platform lacked consistency, lacking visual and interaction consistency."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 bg-accent-3-muted p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"caption-lg","children":"Time Constraints"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Due to the time constraints of the developers, I had to work quickly and efficiently to create a design system that would be easy to use and understand."}]]}]]}]
3:["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","id":"step3","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","h4",null,{"children":"Solution"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 content-width","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Perfecting handoff"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Previously, we had hourly check-ups, which caused a disconnect in the design process. However, due to our short time span, both the deve and I had to this of communicating We switched to Loom, enabling real-time visual updates without interrupting our workflow."}]]}],["$","img",null,{"src":"/images/wizparser/wizparse_FigmaNotes.png","alt":"Final Assets","className":"greyborder my-4 full"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 ","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":" From this, we were able to create a design strategy that would allow for a more efficient and effective design process:"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"blank-bg","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"caption-lg","children":"Past Development Process"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 h-full","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"1. Developer would go and make a new element from scratch without any context or guidance."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"header-border"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"2. Developers would try to figure out how to implement the element in the codebase from the previous developer's code."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"header-border"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"3. Most of production time would be spent on bug fixing and making sure the element is working in the existing code space."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"header-border"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"4. The final element would be added, despite not matching the quality of the rest of the codebase."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"solution-bg","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"caption-lg","children":"New Development Process"}],["$","div",null,{"className":" space-y-4 h-full","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"1. Developers start by looking at the Wiz Parser design system, and see how they can use the components to create a new element."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"header-border"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"2. Developers have direct comments and instructions in the Figma file to help them implement the element in the codebase, outlining typography spacing and breakpoints."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"header-border"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"3. Developers can easily scale and onboard new team members with the design system and documentation"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"header-border"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"4. The final element would be added, matching the quality of the rest of the codebase- creating a more consistent and maintainable codebase."}]]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Here are some of the details I prepared before handoff:"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 content-width","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Typography"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Previously, type styles were not defined, which led to elements having no consistent style. To solve this, a typography guidelines was formed based on the existing fonts—Montserrat and Shantell Sans—allowing for a consistent style across all elements."}]]}],["$","img",null,{"className":"greyborder full","src":"/images/wizparser/Typography.png"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"header-border"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 content-width","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Colours"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The primary and neutral palettes were defined using the Radix color system, allowing for straightforward integration into the Parser's code that would work in both light and dark modes. Naming conventions were based on JSON file systems, allowing easy implementation into the development codebase."}]]}],"$L10"]}],"$L11","$L12"]}],"$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16"]}]
